  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1055 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nSunday night through Friday:\n\nStrong high pressure centered just north of the Great Lakes will \nvery gradually shift eastward Sunday night through Wednesday. A \ncooler and much drier airmass is expected across southern Wisconsin \nthrough this period under the influence of the high and an upper \nlevel troughing pattern. Below normal high and low temps are \nanticipated through mid-week. \n\nLatest forecast models suggest the upper level trough and surface \nhigh will maintain enough of an influence across southern Wisconsin \nfor continued mainly dry weather late week next week, with \ntemperatures gradually returning to near normal by the end of the \nweek as upper level ridging begins to build in from the west. \n\nDDV",
